# docker compose --profile app up: order 8080, payment 8081, inventory 8082

### Confirmed: alice can pay and everything is in stock
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "alice", "items": [{"sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 89.90}, {"sku": "MOUSE", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 24.50}]}

### Cancelled: bob only has EUR 50
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "bob", "items": [{"sku": "MONITOR", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 199.00}]}

### Refunded and cancelled: carol pays, but there are no webcams
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "carol", "items": [{"sku": "WEBCAM", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 59.00}]}

### An order and the steps of its saga (use an id returned above)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### A customer's orders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders?customerId=carol

### Balances
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/accounts/carol

### Stock
GET http://localhost:8082/api/v1/stock

### Restock webcams
PUT http://localhost:8082/api/v1/stock/WEBCAM
Content-Type: application/json

{"available": 10}
